{
  "A set of mutually exclusive options. Options can come from plain values, custom objects or a live list, and can be arranged vertically, horizontally or in columns. Individual options can be disabled, hidden or given help text. The group is a single Tab stop, and the arrow keys move between options.": "",
  "A plain value serves as its own text. `x-model` provides two-way binding for the selected value. When you create the component with `new`, set the same properties programmatically.": "",
  "Binding to data": "",
  "Custom objects use `itemText` and `itemValue`, each a property name or a function. Items can be plain or reactive and are read as they are. After adding, removing or renaming items in place, call `refresh()` to update the display, which preserves focus and selection.": "",
  "Disabled options, help text and hints": "",
  "A `RadioItem` has its own `enabled`, `visible`, `hint` and `helpText`, each a value or a function. The arrow keys skip options that cannot be selected.": "",
  "Orientation and columns": "Yön ve sütunlar",
  "Moves focus into the group, on the selected option or the first available one. The next Tab leaves the group.": "",
  "Moves to the next option and selects it, wrapping from last to first and skipping disabled and hidden options.": "",
  "Moves the same way, backward. On right-to-left pages, ← and → are swapped.": "",
  "Selects the focused option.": "",
  "Moves focus to the group (Control + Option + key on Apple platforms).": "",
  "`role=\"radiogroup\"` named by the field label (`aria-labelledby`), with `aria-orientation`, `aria-required`, `aria-readonly`, `aria-invalid`, and `aria-describedby` for the help text.": "",
  "Native `<input type=\"radio\">` elements sharing a name, each inside its own `<label>` and drawn with `appearance: none`.": "",
  "An option's `helpText` sits outside its label and is linked with `aria-describedby`, so it is not part of the option's name.": "",
  "Native `disabled`: skipped by the keyboard and announced as unavailable.": "",
  "One Tab stop, with the design system focus ring shown only during keyboard use.": "",
  "The group has no strings of its own. The option text is yours, and functions of your language state work. The `required` message comes from `uiLocale.strings`.": "",
  "The field. `data-orientation`, `data-columns`, `data-size`, `data-invalid`, `data-readonly`, `data-disabled`, `data-required`.": "Field. `data-orientation`, `data-columns`, `data-size`, `data-invalid`, `data-readonly`, `data-disabled`, `data-required`.",
  "The `radiogroup` element. `columns` sets `--_columns` and `--_rows` on it.": "",
  "An option, and the label that holds its radio and text.": "",
  "The radio, its text and its help text.": "",
  "Units: the circle in every state (`checked`, `invalid`, `hover`, `pressed`, `focus` and their combinations, `disabled`), and the dot of the selected option (`checked`, `pressed`, `disabled`).": "",
  "Units: an option's row (`hover`, `checked`, `disabled`), its text and its help text.": "",
  "Units: a halo centered on the circle and a ring around an option during keyboard use, where the design language includes them.": "",
  "Units: the options as a group, and the group label when it floats.": "",
  "The circle and the dot, per size and state.": "Boyut ve duruma göre daire ve nokta.",
  "Row height (density tokens) and text size.": "",
  "The space before the text, between side-by-side options, and above an option's help text.": "",
  "The distance the circle moves when pressed, and what the keyboard ring surrounds.": "",
  "The value of the selected item, or `null` if none is selected. `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "The options. A function is tracked, so a new list appears immediately. Items changed in place appear after `refresh()`.": "",
  "Where a custom object stores its text. This is a reader, not a binding.": "",
  "Where an item stores its value. An object without one serves as its own value.": "",
  "The group label. Writing `&Name` makes Alt+N move focus to the group. This is the same property as `text`.": "",
  "`top`, `side` (next to the options) or `hidden` (for screen readers only).": "`top`, `side` (seçeneklerin yanında) ya da `hidden` (yalnız ekran okuyucular için).",
  "`vertical` stacks the options, and `horizontal` places them side by side and wraps.": "",
  "Arranges the options in a grid with this many columns (down the columns when vertical, across when horizontal).": "",
  "Help text shown below the group. An error message replaces it.": "",
  "A tooltip on the group.": "Grup üzerinde bir tooltip.",
  "The arrow keys move between options, but nothing can be selected.": "",
  "An option must be selected.": "",
  "Generated": "",
  "The name the radios submit with the form.": "",
  "RadioItem": "RadioItem",
  "The value of `value` when this option is selected.": "",
  "Shown next to the circle. By default, this is the value as text.": "",
  "A smaller line below the text that describes the radio.": "",
  "`false` dims the option, and the arrow keys skip it.": "",
  "`false` removes the option.": "",
  "The element with `role=\"radiogroup\"`.": "`role=\"radiogroup\"` öğesi.",
  "The native radios, in item order.": "",
  "Sets focus on the selected option, or on the first available one.": "",
  "Your items can be plain or reactive, and the group reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. Their text, values and states are read again, and focus stays where it is.": "",
  "DOM events from the radios bubble up to the group.": ""
}
